    "title": "docs: credit NotRexed for Hookshot, and README.md, docs/BAKE.md, no changelog.txt",
    "body": "The rename to Longshot also rewrote NotRexed's credit (\"NotRexed: Longshot, BlueShell, ...\") and parts of the project's history, as if Longshot were the original. Longshot is a fork of NotRexed's [Hookshot](https://github.com/NotRexed/Hookshot), and the readme, credits and history should say so.\n\n## Credits and history\n\n- **README:** a line under the intro: Longshot is a fork of Hookshot, which NotRexed made, and the history up to the fork is Hookshot's. The Credits section opens with the same statement and credits **NotRexed** for Hookshot (plus BlueShell, Skybound and the a64-kit tools). EvilOOT's link goes back to `evilmfkr/Hookshot` (`evilmfkr/Longshot` is a 404).\n- **License (README):** it says Longshot is a modified version of Hookshot under the same GPL-3.0-or-later, with two notices: `Hookshot: Copyright (C) 2026 NotRexed and the Hookshot contributors` and `Longshot: Copyright (C) 2026 the Longshot contributors`. `LICENSE` is the GPL's text, which carries no project copyright line and may not be changed, so it stays as it is.\n- **CHANGELOG.md:** a note at the top saying the entries up to 2.2.0-rc.1 are Hookshot's releases. The four entries whose text the rename changed (`hookshot_log.txt`, `hookshot-k10`, \"what Hookshot connects to\", `hookshot_env.txt`) are back as they were released. The note goes above the first `## [` heading, so release-please and `release_promote.sh` still insert new entries below it.\n- **Other places the rename rewrote history:** `host/oot_heap_retry.c`, `nx2/oot_patches.py` and `tests/test_oot_heap_retry.py` say `TomShafford/Hookshot (a Hookshot fork)` again, since `TomShafford/Longshot` doesn't exist. `host/PROVENANCE.md` and `gpu/PROVENANCE.md` say where code came from, so they say Hookshot again. The same goes for the measured runs of Hookshot builds in `docs/cpu-profile.md` and `docs/saves.md`, the Fritchii recipe note (\"Not recorded by Hookshot\"), the `vk_vendor.h` comment and two comments in `tests/test_menu_size.py` that quote old version strings.\n- **`docs/development.md`:** the `third_party/` row now says a64-kit's changes are Hookshot's, \"marked `(longshot)` since the rename\".\n\nProduct names, binaries, paths, env vars and the `(longshot)` markers keep the Longshot name.\n\n## Cleanup\n\n- `readme.md` is renamed to `README.md`. Updated: CONTRIBUTING.md, docs (tested-configurations, saves, development), the three tests that read the option table, `scripts/linux/appimage.sh` (copies it into the AppImage), the two workflows' comments, and the opening comment of three `host_shaders/*_spv.h`. `scripts/host_shaders.py` keeps that comment when it regenerates the headers, and `--check` still reports 4 matches.\n- `BAKE.md` moves to `docs/BAKE.md`. Updated: its own table, `gpu/shaderbatch.cpp`, `nx2/bake_mimo.py`, `tests/test_bake_ds.py` and `tests/test_bake_skeleton.py`.\n- `changelog.txt` is deleted. Only docs mentioned it, and nothing built, shipped or read it. `docs/versioning.md` and the 2.0.14 entry in CHANGELOG.md now link Hookshot's own copy (`NotRexed/Hookshot/blob/main/changelog.txt`).\n\n**Overlap with the release/updater work:** the only release-side files touched are `docs/versioning.md` (the changelog.txt paragraph) and comment lines in `linux-appimage.yml` and `windows-builder.yml`. The code that still points at `NotRexed/Longshot` (the update checks, the bug report and pipeline-share issue links, `recomplauncher.json`, the MSI's About link, `-R NotRexed/Longshot` in versioning.md) is left for that work.\n\n## Testing\n\n`python -I -B tests/run_all.py`: 450 passed, 7 failed, 71 skipped, both before and after this change, with the same 7 failures. Five of them come from the sandbox's read-only `/tmp` and pass when run on their own outside it (`test_program_cache_cleanup`, `test_program_cache_one_variant`, `test_control`, `test_longshot_ctl`, `test_vram_budget_row`). The other two already fail on main: `test_bake_portability` (no `zstandard` module here) and `test_builder_log_read_only` (no `libtk8.6`). The checks that read README.md (`test_readme_menu_rows`, `test_stick_dead_zone`, `test_camera_speed`) pass, and so do `test_host_shaders`, `test_oot_heap_retry` and `test_menu_size`.\n\nDocs, comments and file names only, with nothing on screen, so no screenshots and no run in the game.\n",
